<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33825" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑλλην-ισμός</span></b> , ὁ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>imitation of the Greeks,
				Hellenism</i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>2 Ma.</u>
				4.13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>use of a pure Greek style and idiom</i>, as an <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρετὴ λόγου</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Diog.Bab.Stoic.
				3.214
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Po.</u>
				2.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Pron.</u>
				71.25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				1.98
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνιοι λέγουσιν Ἑ. εἶναι τὸν
				ποιητήν</span> (i.e. Homer), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lex.Vind.</u>
				311
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ Ἑλληνισμοῦ</span>, title
			of works by Seleucus, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				9.367a
			</span></i>; by Ptolemy of Ascalon, Philoxenus and Tryphon, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κανόνες Ἑλληνισμοῦ</span>,
			title of work by Irenaeus, Id. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>use of the</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοινή</span>, opp. to strict Atticism,
				<i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1012
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>paganism</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				84a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ τοῦ Ἑ. δυσσέβεια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Cod.Just.</u>
					1.11.9.1
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
